<div class="wrap">
  <section class="spread" aria-labelledby="intro">
    <h1 id="intro">Your 11ty site, built in Rust. Same bytes, sooner.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Brrrty is a static site generator that builds an existing 11ty project and writes the same files 11ty&nbsp;3.1.8 writes, byte for byte. Templates, Markdown and data stay where they are. The config moves from JavaScript to Rhai.</p>
    <div class="account">

      <div class="install">
<pre><code>npm i -D brrrty</code></pre>
        <p>Then <code class="nowrap">"build": "brrrty build"</code> in your <code>package.json</code> scripts. On macOS and Linux. Or, with Rust 1.89 or later, <code class="nowrap">cargo install brrrty</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="next">
        <a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started/">Move a site over</a>
        <a href="/docs/differences/">What's different from 11ty</a>
      </p>
    </div>

